        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "66ce5520-bcd9-59fa-a0e5-c42f25d9179f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pisgah National Forest, Western North Carolina, Haywood County, Transylvania County, Brevard, Asheville\n- Trails: Art Loeb Trail\n- Peaks: Black Balsam Knob, Tennent Mountain, Pilot Mountain, Cold Mountain\n- Organizations: United States Forest Service, United States Department of Agriculture\n- Systems: North Carolina National Forests\n\nFacts:\n- Pisgah National Forest is a national forest in the Appalachian Mountains of western North Carolina.\n- Pisgah National Forest is administered by the United States Forest Service, which is part of the United States Department of Agriculture.\n- Pisgah National Forest is managed with the Croatan, Nantahala, and Uwharrie national forests from a common headquarters in Asheville, North Carolina.\n- The Art Loeb Trail is a 30.1-mile trail in Pisgah National Forest in western North Carolina.\n- The Art Loeb Trail runs from Daniel Boone Boy Scout Camp in Haywood County to an area near Davidson River Campground near Brevard in Transylvania County.\n- The Art Loeb Trail traverses Black Balsam Knob, Tennent Mountain, and Pilot Mountain.\n- The Art Loeb Trail passes the base of Cold Mountain, which was made famous by the novel and film.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4680490f-4f99-5a4b-8faf-a64a702a6ffc",
        "text": "Page: Art Loeb Trail. Sentence: The Art Loeb Trail is a 30.1 mi trail located in Pisgah National Forest in Western North Carolina.\nPage: Art Loeb Trail. Sentence: The northern terminus is at the Daniel Boone Boy Scout Camp in Haywood County, while the trail's southern terminus is located near the Davidson River Campground, near Brevard, in Transylvania County.\nPage: Art Loeb Trail. Sentence: Along the way, the trail traverses several significant peaks, including Black Balsam Knob (6,214 ft), Tennent Mountain (6040 ft) and Pilot Mountain (5095 ft).\nPage: Art Loeb Trail. Sentence: The trail also passes the base of Cold Mountain, made famous by the novel and film.\nPage: Pisgah National Forest. Sentence: Pisgah National Forest is a National Forest in the Appalachian Mountains of western North Carolina.\nPage: Pisgah National Forest. Sentence: It is administered by the United States Forest Service, part of the United States Department of Agriculture.\nPage: Pisgah National Forest. Sentence: The forest is managed together with the other three North Carolina National Forests (Croatan, Nantahala, and Uwharrie) from common headquarters in Asheville, North Carolina.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
